From e3ac602b56b2e8f4002952ea58fd3dfdd97ca918 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Barattolo <barattolo@barattolo.store>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] payment window: cancel an active trade when the buyer's time
 to pay, chosen by the maker, ends

The maker of a sell order chooses on the marketplace how long the buyer has
to send the fiat once the trade is active (a timer, whole minutes from 15
minutes to 24 hours). This daemon
asks the marketplace server for the window of each trade newly active (a job
of its own, every minute, outside the serial message loop), stamps the
moment it saw the trade active, and when the window ends with the order still
active cancels the hold invoice exactly as the escrow guardian does, and
tells the server (expired / payment-window).

Only whole minutes from 900 to 86400 seconds are accepted; fiat-sent and disputes are never
touched. Inert without BARATTOLO_FINESTRA_URL and BARATTOLO_FINESTRA_SEGRETO.
